---
title: 'Org Chart'
enterprise: true
---

An Organisation Chart displays hierarchical relationships between people, departments, or entities as a
tree of connected cards. Each card can contain structured content such as names, job titles, and images.

{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/display-mode-full.svg" alt="Organisation Chart" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}

The Organisation Series is an enterprise feature and is created using the `organization` series type.

## Basic Setup

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            data: [
                { id: 'ceo', name: 'CEO', parentId: null },
                { id: 'cto', name: 'CTO', parentId: 'ceo' },
                { id: 'cfo', name: 'CFO', parentId: 'ceo' },
                { id: 'dev', name: 'Dev Lead', parentId: 'cto' },
                { id: 'qa', name: 'QA Lead', parentId: 'cto' },
                { id: 'acc', name: 'Accountant', parentId: 'cfo' },
            ],
            idKey: 'id',
            parentIdKey: 'parentId',
        },
    ],
}
```

The `idKey` and `parentIdKey` properties define the parent-child relationships between nodes. Each row in the
data represents a single node, with its parent identified by `parentIdKey`. The root node has a `null` parent.

Sibling order follows the order nodes appear in the data array.

## Data Model

Each data row represents a node in the hierarchy. All node properties — names, titles, images — are included
directly on the record alongside the `id` and `parentId` fields. The `image` field works like the
[Image fill](/options/) options, accepting a URL string.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            data: [
                { id: 1, name: 'Alice Chen', jobTitle: 'CEO', image: 'alice.png', parentId: null },
                { id: 2, name: 'Bob Smith', jobTitle: 'CTO', image: 'bob.png', parentId: 1 },
                { id: 3, name: 'Carol Wu', jobTitle: 'CFO', image: 'carol.png', parentId: 1 },
                { id: 4, name: 'Dave Jones', jobTitle: 'Dev Lead', image: 'dave.png', parentId: 2 },
                { id: 5, name: 'Eve Park', jobTitle: 'QA Lead', image: 'eve.png', parentId: 2 },
            ],
            idKey: 'id',
            parentIdKey: 'parentId',
            title: { key: 'name' },
            subtitle: { key: 'jobTitle' },
            image: { key: 'image' },
        },
    ],
}
```

When names are unique, they can serve as the ID directly — no separate numeric `id` field needed.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            data: [
                { name: 'Alice Chen', jobTitle: 'CEO', image: 'alice.png', manager: null },
                { name: 'Bob Smith', jobTitle: 'CTO', image: 'bob.png', manager: 'Alice Chen' },
                { name: 'Carol Wu', jobTitle: 'CFO', image: 'carol.png', manager: 'Alice Chen' },
                { name: 'Dave Jones', jobTitle: 'Dev Lead', image: 'dave.png', manager: 'Bob Smith' },
                { name: 'Eve Park', jobTitle: 'QA Lead', image: 'eve.png', manager: 'Bob Smith' },
            ],
            idKey: 'name',
            parentIdKey: 'manager',
            title: { key: 'name' },
            subtitle: { key: 'jobTitle' },
            image: { key: 'image' },
        },
    ],
}
```

## Node Presentation

Each card in the chart can display a `title`, `subtitle`, additional `label` fields, and an `image`.

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true %}

{% tabItem id="image-left" label="Left" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/image-position-left.svg" alt="Organisation chart with images on the left of each card" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="image-top" label="Top" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/image-position-top.svg" alt="Organisation chart with images at the top of each card" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="image-right" label="Right" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/image-position-right.svg" alt="Organisation chart with images on the right of each card" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="image-bottom" label="Bottom" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/image-position-bottom.svg" alt="Organisation chart with images at the bottom of each card" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% /tabs %}

### Title and Subtitle

The `title` and `subtitle` are always visible, including in compact display mode.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            title: { key: 'name', fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold' },
            subtitle: { key: 'jobTitle', fontSize: 12, color: '#666' },
        },
    ],
}
```

### Labels

Additional information can be displayed using the `label` array. Each entry maps a data field via its
`key` and is stacked vertically below the subtitle.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            title: { key: 'name' },
            subtitle: { key: 'jobTitle' },
            label: [
                { key: 'department', fontSize: 11, color: '#888' },
                { key: 'location', fontSize: 11, color: '#888' },
            ],
        },
    ],
}
```

Labels are hidden in compact display mode. Each label supports a `styler` callback for per-node
text customisation.

### Image

Cards can include an image, such as a profile photo. The `image` property supports configuring the
shape, size, and position within the card.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            image: {
                key: 'photoUrl',
                shape: 'circle',
                width: 48,
                height: 48,
                position: 'left',
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The `position` property controls where the image appears within the card. The `shape` can be
`'circle'` or `'square'`.

## Display Mode

The `displayMode` property controls how much detail each card shows.

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true %}

{% tabItem id="display-full" label="Full" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/display-mode-full.svg" alt="Organisation chart in full display mode showing all card content" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="display-compact" label="Compact" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/display-mode-compact.svg" alt="Organisation chart in compact display mode showing title and subtitle only" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% /tabs %}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            displayMode: 'auto',
        },
    ],
}
```

-   `'full'` — Shows all content: title, subtitle, labels, and image.
-   `'compact'` — Shows only the title and subtitle. Labels and images are hidden.
-   `'auto'` (default) — Automatically switches between full and compact based on available space.

## Layout

The `direction` property controls the orientation of the chart.

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true %}

{% tabItem id="layout-vertical" label="Vertical" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/layout-top-to-bottom.svg" alt="Organisation chart with vertical (top to bottom) layout" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="layout-horizontal" label="Horizontal" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/layout-left-to-right.svg" alt="Organisation chart with horizontal (left to right) layout" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% /tabs %}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            direction: 'vertical',
        },
    ],
}
```

The available values are `'vertical'` (default) and `'horizontal'`. In right-to-left (RTL) locales,
the horizontal layout is automatically mirrored.

## Connectors

Connectors are the lines drawn between parent and child nodes. They are configured through the `link`
property.

### Interpolation

The `link.interpolation.type` property controls the shape of the connectors. When using `'step'`
connectors, the `cornerRadius` property rounds the corners where the horizontal line drops down toward children.

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true %}

{% tabItem id="connector-elbow" label="Step" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/connectors-step.svg" alt="Organisation chart with step connectors using right-angle routing" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="connector-step-rounded" label="Step (Rounded)" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/connectors-step-rounded.svg" alt="Organisation chart with step connectors using rounded corners" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="connector-smooth" label="Smooth" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/connectors-smooth.svg" alt="Organisation chart with smooth Bezier curve connectors" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="connector-linear" label="Linear" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/connectors-linear.svg" alt="Organisation chart with straight diagonal connectors" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% /tabs %}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            link: {
                interpolation: {
                    type: 'step',
                    cornerRadius: 8,
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

-   `'step'` (default) — Orthogonal connectors with right-angle routing. Use `cornerRadius` to round the corners where the horizontal line breaks off downward toward children.
-   `'smooth'` — Bezier curve connectors. The `tension` property (0–1) controls the curve tightness.
-   `'linear'` — Straight diagonal lines between nodes.

### Connector Styling

Connectors can be styled globally or per-connector using the `link.itemStyler` callback.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            link: {
                stroke: '#999',
                strokeWidth: 2,
                lineDash: [4, 2],
                itemStyler: ({ datum }) => {
                    if (datum.relationship === 'dotted-line') {
                        return { lineDash: [4, 2], stroke: '#ccc' };
                    }
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The `itemStyler` callback receives the parent and child data for each connector, allowing
conditional styling based on relationship data.

## Collapse and Expand

Nodes with children can be collapsed and expanded. The indicator shows the direct child count when
collapsed.

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true %}

{% tabItem id="badge-expanded" label="Badge (Expanded)" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/expander-badge-expanded.svg" alt="Organisation chart fully expanded with no badges" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="badge-collapsed" label="Badge (Collapsed)" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/expander-badge-collapsed.svg" alt="Organisation chart with collapsed nodes showing yellow circle badges with child count" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="pill-expanded" label="Pill (Expanded)" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/expander-pill-expanded.svg" alt="Organisation chart fully expanded with outlined pill indicators" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% tabItem id="pill-collapsed" label="Pill (Collapsed)" %}
{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/expander-pill-collapsed.svg" alt="Organisation chart with collapsed nodes showing filled pills with child count" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}
{% /tabItem %}

{% /tabs %}

### Badge Styling

The collapse/expand badge is a circular indicator positioned at the bottom of the card. When collapsed,
it displays the direct child count. It is configured through the `badge` property.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            badge: {
                fill: '#3366CC',
                stroke: '#3366CC',
                color: '#FFFFFF',
                fontSize: 11,
                cornerRadius: 12,
                styler: ({ datum, expanded, childCount }) => {
                    if (expanded) {
                        return { fill: 'transparent' };
                    }
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The `styler` callback receives the node's `datum`, `expanded` state, and `childCount`, allowing
per-node customisation of the badge.

An alternative pill-shaped expander is also under consideration, with a similar set of configuration
properties.

### Initial State

The `initialState` property controls which nodes are expanded when the chart first renders. It accepts a
list of expanded node IDs. When a node is listed as expanded, all its ancestors up to the root are
automatically opened to ensure the node is visible.

This uses the same state format as `getState()` and `setState()` described below.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            initialState: {
                expanded: ['ceo', 'cto'],
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

> **Note:** An alternative approach would be to specify collapsed nodes instead — listing nodes whose
> children should be hidden, with all other nodes open by default. This could be useful for "start fully
> expanded, then close specific branches" scenarios.

### Programmatic Control

The chart state can be read and updated programmatically using `getState()` and `setState()`.
The state format is the same as `initialState`.

```js
// Read the current expand/collapse state
const state = chart.getState();
// state.expanded = ['ceo', 'cto', ...]

// Set specific expanded nodes (ancestors are auto-expanded)
chart.setState({ expanded: ['ceo', 'cto', 'dev-lead'] });
```

## Highlighting

Hovering over a node highlights the tree path — the node itself, its ancestors, and its descendants.
Nodes and connectors outside the highlighted path are dimmed.

{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/highlight-tree-path.svg" alt="Tree path highlighting showing ancestors and descendants" maxWidth="80%" constrained=true centered=true enableDarkModeFilter=true /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            highlightStyle: {
                item: {
                    fill: '#E3F2FD',
                    stroke: '#1565C0',
                    strokeWidth: 2,
                },
                unhighlightedBranch: {
                    opacity: 0.3,
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The `highlightStyle.item` controls the appearance of highlighted nodes, while
`highlightStyle.unhighlightedBranch` styles the dimmed nodes outside the path.

## Tooltips

Tooltips are disabled by default. When enabled, they display all label fields for the hovered node.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            tooltip: {
                enabled: true,
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

A `tooltip.renderer` callback can be used for custom formatting. The renderer receives the node's
`datum`, `depth`, `childCount`, and all configured label values.

## Event Handling

The `nodeClick` event fires when a node card is clicked, providing the node's data and tree context.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            listeners: {
                nodeClick: (event) => {
                    console.log('Clicked:', event.datum);
                    console.log('Depth:', event.depth);
                    console.log('Expanded:', event.isExpanded);
                    console.log('Children:', event.childCount);
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The event payload includes:

-   `datum` — The data object for the clicked node.
-   `depth` — The depth of the node in the tree (root = 0).
-   `isExpanded` — Whether the node is currently expanded.
-   `childCount` — The number of direct children.

## Customisation

### Node Styling

The `itemStyler` callback provides per-node visual customisation based on data and tree state.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            itemStyler: ({ datum, depth, isExpanded, displayMode, highlighted }) => {
                if (depth === 0) {
                    return { fill: '#1565C0', stroke: '#0D47A1' };
                }
                if (datum.department === 'Engineering') {
                    return { fill: '#E8F5E9', stroke: '#43A047' };
                }
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

The callback receives:

-   `datum` — The node's data object.
-   `depth` — The node's depth in the tree.
-   `isExpanded` — Whether the node is expanded.
-   `displayMode` — The current display mode (`'compact'` or `'full'`).
-   `highlighted` — Whether the node is in the highlighted path.

It can return: `fill`, `stroke`, `strokeWidth`, `opacity`, `cornerRadius`, `lineDash`.

### Label Styling

Each label in the `label` array supports a `styler` callback for per-node text customisation.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'organization',
            label: [
                {
                    key: 'department',
                    styler: ({ datum }) => {
                        if (datum.department === 'Engineering') {
                            return { color: '#2E7D32', fontWeight: 'bold' };
                        }
                    },
                },
            ],
        },
    ],
}
```

## Navigation

Large organisation charts often exceed the visible area. Click and drag on the chart background to pan
across the hierarchy.

The viewport automatically centres on the root node when the chart first renders. After expanding or
collapsing a node, the view adjusts to keep the interacted node visible.

{% note %}
Zoom (via mouse wheel) is planned for a future release.
{% /note %}

## Keyboard Navigation

Organisation Charts support keyboard navigation for accessibility. See the [Accessibility](./accessibility/) page for details.

## API Reference

```js
interface AgOrganizationSeriesOptions {
    type: 'organization';

    /** Array of node records. Each record represents one node in the hierarchy. */
    data?: object[];
    /** Key in data for the unique node identifier. Default: `'id'`. */
    idKey?: string;
    /** Key in data for the parent node identifier. Default: `'parentId'`. */
    parentIdKey?: string;

    /** Primary text field, always visible. */
    title?: {
        key: string;
        fontSize?: number;
        fontWeight?: CSSFontWeight;
        fontFamily?: string;
        color?: string;
        styler?: (params: OrganizationLabelStylerParams) => OrganizationLabelStyle;
    };
    /** Secondary text field, always visible. */
    subtitle?: {
        key: string;
        fontSize?: number;
        fontWeight?: CSSFontWeight;
        fontFamily?: string;
        color?: string;
        styler?: (params: OrganizationLabelStylerParams) => OrganizationLabelStyle;
    };
    /** Additional text fields, hidden in compact mode. */
    label?: Array<{
        key: string;
        fontSize?: number;
        fontWeight?: CSSFontWeight;
        fontFamily?: string;
        color?: string;
        styler?: (params: OrganizationLabelStylerParams) => OrganizationLabelStyle;
    }>;
    /** Image displayed within each card. */
    image?: {
        /** Key in node data for the image URL. */
        key: string;
        /** Shape of the image mask. Default: `'square'`. */
        shape?: 'circle' | 'square';
        /** Width of the image in pixels. */
        width?: number;
        /** Height of the image in pixels. */
        height?: number;
        /** How the image fills its container. Default: `'cover'`. */
        fit?: 'cover' | 'contain' | 'fill';
        /** Position of the image within the card. Default: `'left'`. */
        position?: 'top' | 'left' | 'bottom' | 'right';
    };

    /** Tree layout direction. Default: `'vertical'`. */
    direction?: 'vertical' | 'horizontal';
    /** Card detail level. Default: `'auto'`. */
    displayMode?: 'compact' | 'full' | 'auto';

    /** Minimum width of each node card (pixels). */
    minWidth?: number;
    /** Maximum width of each node card (pixels). */
    maxWidth?: number;
    /** Fixed height of each node card (pixels). */
    height?: number;
    /** Maximum height of each node card (pixels). */
    maxHeight?: number;
    /** Minimum spacing between nodes (pixels). */
    minSpacing?: number;

    /** Connector line configuration. */
    link?: {
        interpolation?: {
            /** Connector shape. Default: `'step'`. */
            type?: 'step' | 'smooth' | 'linear';
            /** Corner rounding where horizontal breaks off downward (pixels). */
            cornerRadius?: number;
            /** Curve tightness for smooth connectors (0–1). */
            tension?: number;
        };
        stroke?: string;
        strokeWidth?: number;
        lineDash?: number[];
        /** Per-connector styling callback. */
        itemStyler?: (params: OrganizationLinkStylerParams) => OrganizationLinkStyle;
        tooltip?: {
            enabled?: boolean;
        };
    };

    /** Initial expand/collapse state. Same format as getState()/setState(). */
    initialState?: {
        /** List of expanded node IDs. Ancestors of listed nodes are auto-expanded. */
        expanded?: Array<string | number>;
    };

    /** Tree-path highlight styling on hover. */
    highlightStyle?: {
        /** Style applied to the hovered node and its ancestors/descendants. */
        item?: {
            fill?: string;
            stroke?: string;
            strokeWidth?: number;
        };
        /** Style applied to nodes outside the highlighted path. */
        unhighlightedBranch?: {
            opacity?: number;
            fill?: string;
            stroke?: string;
        };
    };

    tooltip?: {
        /** Whether to show tooltips on node hover. Default: `false`. */
        enabled?: boolean;
    };

    /** Per-node card styling callback. */
    itemStyler?: (params: OrganizationItemStylerParams) => OrganizationItemStyle;

    listeners?: {
        /** Fired when a node card is clicked. */
        nodeClick?: (event: OrganizationNodeClickEvent) => void;
    };
}
```
